# ExamDash Check-in API — HTTP Collection
# Week 5 | Backend Engineering | Build Prize Labs EIP
# Base URL: https://examdash-checkin-api-1.onrender.com
#
# HOW TO USE:
# 1. Run the Signup request first to create an account
# 2. Run Login to get your token
# 3. Copy the token value and paste it into the @token variable below
# 4. Run any protected request

@baseUrl = https://examdash-checkin-api-1.onrender.com
@token = PASTE_YOUR_TOKEN_HERE

# ============================================================
# AUTH — PUBLIC ROUTES (no token needed)
# ============================================================

### 1. Signup — Create a new learner account
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "ada@examdash.com",
  "password": "password123",
  "role": "learner"
}

###

### 2. Signup — Create a reviewer account
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "reviewer@examdash.com",
  "password": "password123",
  "role": "reviewer"
}

###

### 3. Login — Get JWT token
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "ada@examdash.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

###

### 4. Login — Wrong password (expect 401)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "ada@examdash.com",
  "password": "wrongpassword"
}

###

# ============================================================
# CHECK-INS — PROTECTED ROUTES (token required)
# ============================================================

### 5. GET all check-ins (learner sees own only)
GET {{baseUrl}}/checkins
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### 6. GET check-ins filtered by track
GET {{baseUrl}}/checkins?track=Backend
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### 7. GET check-ins filtered by status
GET {{baseUrl}}/checkins?status=pending
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### 8. GET check-ins with pagination
GET {{baseUrl}}/checkins?page=1&limit=5
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### 9. GET check-ins sorted by submitted_at
GET {{baseUrl}}/checkins?sort=submitted_at
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### 10. GET single check-in by ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/checkins/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### 11. GET check-in that belongs to another user (expect 403)
GET {{baseUrl}}/checkins/999
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### 12. POST — Create a new check-in
POST {{baseUrl}}/checkins
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "learner_name": "Ada Okafor",
  "track": "Backend",
  "status": "pending",
  "submitted_at": "2026-05-08T10:00:00Z"
}

###

### 13. POST — Missing required field (expect 400 validation error)
POST {{baseUrl}}/checkins
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "track": "Backend",
  "status": "pending"
}

###

### 14. POST — Invalid track value (expect 400 validation error)
POST {{baseUrl}}/checkins
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "learner_name": "Ada Okafor",
  "track": "InvalidTrack",
  "status": "pending",
  "submitted_at": "2026-05-08T10:00:00Z"
}

###

### 15. PATCH — Update status only
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/checkins/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "submitted"
}

###

### 16. PATCH — Update multiple fields
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/checkins/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "reviewed",
  "learner_name": "Ada O."
}

###

### 17. DELETE — Delete a check-in (expect 204)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/checkins/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### 18. GET with no token (expect 401)
GET {{baseUrl}}/checkins

###

### 19. GET with invalid token (expect 401)
GET {{baseUrl}}/checkins
Authorization: Bearer invalidtoken123

###
